<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu Sa'id Bahadur Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1335</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Abu Saʿid</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu Sa'id Bahadur Khan was the last effective ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a>, the Mongol state centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>. His reign saw peace with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluks</a> but also rivalry among powerful <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amir">amirs</a>. When he died without an heir in 1335, the Ilkhanate rapidly fragmented among competing factions and regional dynasties.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abu-said-bahadur-khan.jpg" alt="Abu Sa'id Bahadur Khan" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: www.numisbids.com · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abu_sa%27id.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
